  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercise_type\": \"CEFR English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"The concept of 'dark tourism' has been gaining popularity in recent years. It refers to the practice of visiting places associated with death, suffering, and tragedy. Such destinations can range from concentration camps during World War II to sites of natural disasters like Pompeii. Proponents argue that these visits provide a unique opportunity for reflection on human history and the consequences of conflict.\n\nHowever, critics point out that dark tourism often exploits the suffering of others for entertainment purposes. They claim that visitors are more concerned with taking selfies in front of memorials than with genuinely engaging with the historical significance of the site. This raises questions about the ethics of such tourism and whether it is respectful to those who suffered at these locations.\n\nIn recent years, dark tourism has become a significant contributor to local economies, with some destinations even offering guided tours that cater specifically to this market. As the industry continues to grow, it is essential for visitors to be aware of their own motivations and the impact they may have on the sites they visit.\",\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 36,\n      \"question\": \"What does the term 'dark tourism' refer to?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Visiting places associated with natural beauty\", \"Traveling to destinations for entertainment purposes\", \"Exploring locations connected to death, suffering, and tragedy\", \"Taking guided tours of historical sites\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Exploring locations connected to death, suffering, and tragedy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 37,\n      \"question\": \"According to the text, what is one of the main concerns of critics regarding dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"That it provides a unique opportunity for reflection on human history\", \"That visitors are more concerned with taking selfies than engaging with historical significance\", \"That it does not contribute significantly to local economies\", \"That it is respectful to those who suffered at these locations\"],\n      \"answer\": \"That visitors are more concerned with taking selfies than engaging with historical significance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 38,\n      \"question\": \"What is mentioned as a potential consequence of dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The desecration of memorials\", \"The exploitation of suffering for entertainment purposes\", \"The decline in local economies\", \"The increase in tourism revenue\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The exploitation of suffering for entertainment purposes\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 39,\n      \"question\": \"What is the author's attitude towards dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"Neutral and informative\", \"Critical and disapproving\", \"Supportive and encouraging\", \"Ambivalent and uncertain\"],\n      \"answer\": \"Critical and disapproving\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"question_number\": 40,\n      \"question\": \"What is mentioned as a growing concern for dark tourism?\",\n      \"options\": [\"The impact on local economies\", \"The respect shown to those who suffered at these locations\", \"The ethics of such tourism\", \"The awareness of visitors' motivations\"],\n      \"answer\": \"The awareness of visitors' motivations\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
